I mean, 'cause vitamin D
has been argued for a cure

00:20:56.187 --> 00:20:58.730
or preventive for everything,

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.530
cancer, strokes, heart attacks.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.178
I mean, this is the even medicine.

00:21:02.178 --> 00:21:03.127
- I don't know where they.

00:21:03.127 --> 00:21:05.520
- That's right, even falls,
that's right, that's right.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:08.060
- So there were some
recommendations early on

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:10.950
that were shocking to me
and skin health, everything,

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:15.040
but no one wanted to
believe that taking vitamins

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.260
can actually lead to more harm.

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:19.560
And I think your book
illuminates both of those points.

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:22.350
Can you tell us we're
taking supplements outside

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:25.950
of taking supplements that have arsenic

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.540
or some other toxic elements to them,

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:31.060
but vitamins on their own can be harmful.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:31.900
Tell us about that.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:35.180
- Well, it's obviously vitamins
are critical, vital life.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:38.070
I mean, you need vitamins are substances

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:40.290
which your body needs, but
cannot make on its own.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:42.940
You need vitamins that's not the issue.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.840
The issue is how best to get them.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.912
And the answer is the best
way to get them is from food.

00:21:47.912 --> 00:21:51.410
I give credit to the
nutritional supplement companies

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:55.160
for being able to sell
what they sell as natural

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.230
because it's not natural.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:58.930
That's not how your body is
meant to take in vitamins

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:01.550
in a compressed pill
that has a large quantity

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:03.420
of vitamin that is not associated

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:05.540
with the other phytochemicals
that are typically found

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:06.990
in vegetables and fruits.

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:09.470
And when you do it that way,
you're not preventing it,

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:10.620
presenting it in natural, right.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:12.590
You're presenting it in an unnatural way,

00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:14.170
which can then have consequences.

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:16.530
And that's what we found
out now that the vitamin C

00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:18.770
can have consequences when
taking large quantities.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:20.870
So can vitamin D, et
cetera, vitamin E, I mean.

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:24.150
So it surprises me they
don't have black box warnings

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:26.090
on them and they would have
black box warnings on them

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:27.510
for these sort of multivitamins

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:31.270
or the sort of high level of
vitamins that people take.

00:22:31.270 --> 00:22:33.090
If the FDA was able to regulate them.

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:36.110
But that Dietary Supplement
Health and Education Act

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:38.710
pushed back against the FDA on this.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.390
And so the FDA doesn't
really regulate them

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:42.500
the way they should, so people don't know.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.550
And that's what was also
interesting to me is just,

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:48.040
here, you talk about going
up against the zeitgeist

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:49.990
of the current culture of
the desire to take a pill,

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.910
but go up against these
nutritional supplement companies.

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:55.320
I mean, they have an
enormous amount of money

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:59.200
and influence and I just
feel so sorry for the patient

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:01.200
who's caught up in all this.

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:05.650
- Because I think people push
towards the supplement space

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:06.483
for two reasons.

00:23:06.483 --> 00:23:07.950
One, they think it's natural,

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:10.240
which is incorrect as you put right now.

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:14.420
And the second is that
they believe against

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:15.400
pharma companies.

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:18.090
They have a negative biased
view of pharma companies,

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:18.923
which is important.

00:23:18.923 --> 00:23:20.940
I think we need to take
a skeptical look about

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:23.610
how pharma companies do their
testing, their approvals,

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:25.470
their pricing especially.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.670
But the reality of pharma
companies getting rich off

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:30.280
of selling a certain medications.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:31.600
And the point you brought up,

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:34.850
which I think is an understated
point that pharma companies

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:37.020
love creating drugs
that patients would take

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.080
for years upon years and daily,
as opposed to finding cures,

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:44.270
as opposed to finding the
new antibiotic is probably

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.370
the worst form of how pharma functions.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:50.840
But these nutritional supplement
companies that pawn off

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:53.430
their supplements as natural are also

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:54.920
billion dollar entities

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:58.220
just like the pharma companies,
except with no regulation

00:23:58.220 --> 00:24:00.350
like they're both billionaire companies.

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:05.350
One is forced to prove
that their medications work

00:24:05.430 --> 00:24:07.140
or what their side effects can be.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.490
And one has free reign
to do whatever they want.

00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:11.580
And yet the public doesn't scrutinize

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:13.000
the nutritional companies at all.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:13.880
- It's amazing.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.120
I mean, I'm on the FDA Vaccine
Advisor Committee, right?

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:19.610
So we sit down and we did
say in December 10th or 17th,

00:24:19.610 --> 00:24:22.130
take over Pfizer's vaccine
and then Moderna's vaccine,

00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:25.390
those were 40,000 person
studies, 30,000 person studies.

00:24:25.390 --> 00:24:28.480
You know, where you get a
200 pages of material to read

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:29.650
before you go through the meeting,

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:32.260
where you look at every piece
of data in terms of safety

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:33.093
and efficacy.

00:24:33.093 --> 00:24:35.880
And then, and only then do you
make sort of a recommendation

00:24:35.880 --> 00:24:37.210
to move forward on those vaccines

00:24:37.210 --> 00:24:40.600
and then nutritional supplement
companies just make it up.

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:43.340
I mean, what's on the label
doesn't necessarily have

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.870
to be what's in the bottle
and people feel much more

00:24:45.870 --> 00:24:48.540
comfortable with that
than they do with this

00:24:48.540 --> 00:24:52.660
highly regulated, highly
supervised and scrutinized process.

00:24:52.660 --> 00:24:53.493
It is remarkable.

00:24:53.493 --> 00:24:56.410
I give credit to these
companies for having sold us

00:24:56.410 --> 00:24:57.243
a bill of goods.

00:24:57.243 --> 00:24:59.440
And I also give credit to mother nature.

00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:02.670
I don't know who her
public relations team is,

00:25:02.670 --> 00:25:05.740
but I wanna hire that group
because she has been trying

00:25:05.740 --> 00:25:06.770
to kill us ever since

00:25:06.770 --> 00:25:08.980
we crawled out of the ocean on the land.

00:25:08.980 --> 00:25:11.330
I mean, when people say we'll
go, so as far as to say,

00:25:11.330 --> 00:25:14.213
they wanna have like a
natural COVID infection,

00:25:14.213 --> 00:25:17.580
as you know, because that's
better than getting a vaccine.

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:20.530
- Yeah, look, in some
ways like a natural fever

00:25:20.530 --> 00:25:22.680
is better than blocking a fever.

00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:24.420
So I kind of see where that started,

00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:27.180
but then there's like this
element of concept creep,

00:25:27.180 --> 00:25:29.340
which Jonathan Height talks about so well

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:32.060
where natural can be better.

00:25:32.060 --> 00:25:33.640
It doesn't mean that it's always better.

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:36.680
And you know certain toxins are natural,

00:25:36.680 --> 00:25:38.440
doesn't mean that we
should be taking them in.

00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:41.470
Dr. Offit sits on the FDA
Vaccine Advisory Committee,

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:44.750
which means he advises the FDA
on which vaccines to approve

00:25:44.750 --> 00:25:45.650
or not approve.

00:25:45.650 --> 00:25:48.390
Which is why I found it so
interesting to learn how critical

00:25:48.390 --> 00:25:51.620
he is of both the Biden
and Trump administrations,

00:25:51.620 --> 00:25:53.750
politicization of health guidance.

00:25:53.750 --> 00:25:57.230
Do you think that a part of
this is the loss of trust

00:25:57.230 --> 00:25:58.760
in medical institutions?

00:25:58.760 --> 00:25:59.870
- Oh, certainly.

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:03.330
Absolutely, and I think
that wasn't always true.

00:26:03.330 --> 00:26:05.860
I mean, I was a child of the fifties

00:26:05.860 --> 00:26:07.189
and I'll give you a perfect example.

00:26:07.189 --> 00:26:11.000
When Jonas Salk made his polio vaccine.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.110
He took the virus, grew it up in cells

00:26:15.110 --> 00:26:16.480
in the laboratory, he purified it,

00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:18.090
he killed it with the
chemical formaldehyde.

00:26:18.090 --> 00:26:20.183
So it was a whole killed viral vaccine.

00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:23.680
And then five companies
stepped forward to make it.

00:26:23.680 --> 00:26:25.060
One of them made it badly,

00:26:25.060 --> 00:26:27.310
Cutter Laboratories of
Berkeley, California

00:26:27.310 --> 00:26:29.913
failed to fully inactivate the polio virus

00:26:29.913 --> 00:26:31.050
that was in their vaccine.

00:26:31.050 --> 00:26:31.897
It's a consequence,

00:26:31.897 --> 00:26:35.980
120,000 children primarily
in the West and Southwest

00:26:35.980 --> 00:26:38.640
were inoculated with live fully virulent,

00:26:38.640 --> 00:26:40.400
fully dangerous polio virus.

00:26:40.400 --> 00:26:42.810
40,000 developed short-lived polio,

00:26:42.810 --> 00:26:44.370
meaning temporary paralysis.

00:26:44.370 --> 00:26:47.880
164 were permanently paralyzed
for the rest of their life.

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:49.060
And 10 were killed.

00:26:49.060 --> 00:26:52.010
I think it was the single
worst biological disaster

00:26:52.010 --> 00:26:53.060
in this country's history.

00:26:53.060 --> 00:26:56.410
And in no sense, shook
faith in the polio vaccine.

00:26:56.410 --> 00:26:59.130
People generally believed
the companies were trying

00:26:59.130 --> 00:27:00.170
to do their best.

00:27:00.170 --> 00:27:02.920
If you looked at the exit
interviews from all the original,

00:27:02.920 --> 00:27:06.677
those early lawsuits against
Cutter, you would see that

00:27:07.770 --> 00:27:09.160
the people who were sitting on those rooms

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:10.480
saw what this was,

00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:12.870
which was a scale up incident
that we just hadn't figured

00:27:12.870 --> 00:27:14.950
out how to mass produce that vaccine yet.

00:27:14.950 --> 00:27:19.950
And wanted to find Cutter
not guilty, not responsible

00:27:19.960 --> 00:27:24.290
amazingly enough but and because
they trusted the companies,

00:27:24.290 --> 00:27:25.420
they trusted the government,

00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:28.520
they trusted the medical
community and something changed.

00:27:28.520 --> 00:27:31.020
I think in the sixties and
seventies, something changed.

00:27:31.020 --> 00:27:34.050
I mean, it became much more
cynical, much more litigious,

00:27:34.050 --> 00:27:36.470
sort of what I call kind of
the post Watergate phenomenon,

00:27:36.470 --> 00:27:39.350
where we saw that there were
sort of evil forces lurking

00:27:39.350 --> 00:27:42.100
behind the curtains,
whether it's Pentagon papers

00:27:42.100 --> 00:27:44.525
or the Nixon tapes when
there was a loss of trust.

00:27:44.525 --> 00:27:47.751
- Yeah, do you think the CDC or the FDA

00:27:47.751 --> 00:27:50.840
can be functioning in a more
effective way when it comes

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:52.930
to communication with the general public,

00:27:52.930 --> 00:27:56.170
whether it's about vaccines
or vitamin supplements,

00:27:56.170 --> 00:27:59.390
because it feels like
there's somehow a gap.

00:27:59.390 --> 00:28:00.800
The FDA makes statements,

00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:03.360
you have medical experts go
on good morning, America,

00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:06.550
et cetera, but yet the
efficacy isn't there.

00:28:06.550 --> 00:28:08.610
It's almost like how we talk about

00:28:08.610 --> 00:28:10.840
some of the things you
mentioned in your book.

00:28:10.840 --> 00:28:13.620
We do them just to do them
with no evidence behind them.

00:28:13.620 --> 00:28:16.067
If the FDA issues a press
release and no one reads it

00:28:16.067 --> 00:28:17.870
and it changes, no one's mind,

00:28:17.870 --> 00:28:20.620
shouldn't we be looking at
other ways of communicating with

00:28:20.620 --> 00:28:21.453
the general public.

00:28:21.453 --> 00:28:24.530
- Yes, I think there has
been during COVID especially

00:28:24.530 --> 00:28:27.050
there has been a real loss
of trust in the public

00:28:27.050 --> 00:28:30.250
health agents, agencies and
public health officials.

00:28:30.250 --> 00:28:32.480
I think, and at some level deservedly so.

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:36.150
I think that if you look at
what happened in the previous

00:28:36.150 --> 00:28:39.020
administration and president
Trump's administration,

00:28:39.020 --> 00:28:41.270
what you saw was you saw
that the administration could

00:28:41.270 --> 00:28:45.120
actually arm twist the FDA,
arm twist them into approving

00:28:45.120 --> 00:28:48.030
through emergency use
authorization hydroxychloroquine.

00:28:48.030 --> 00:28:50.630
An anti-malarial drug that
had never been shown to work,

00:28:50.630 --> 00:28:53.823
to either treat or prevent
COVID, and they approved that.

00:28:53.823 --> 00:28:55.750
I mean, they, three months later,

00:28:55.750 --> 00:28:59.250
they took away the approval
when it was shown not to work

00:28:59.250 --> 00:29:02.300
and shown to have heart
arrhythmias, which could be fatal.

00:29:02.300 --> 00:29:04.870
But that really shook people's confidence.

00:29:04.870 --> 00:29:08.500
I mean, so much so that before
the vaccine was released

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:11.890
in December, people were so worried about

00:29:11.890 --> 00:29:13.470
what the Trump administration would do

00:29:13.470 --> 00:29:15.470
was that states didn't trust the FDA

00:29:15.470 --> 00:29:17.330
or the FDA Vaccine Advisory Committee

00:29:17.330 --> 00:29:19.280
and formed their own advisory committees.

00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:20.750
That's how bad it was.

00:29:20.750 --> 00:29:22.990
Also, I do think now, for example,

00:29:22.990 --> 00:29:26.220
if fantasies could come true,
I would like to do what,

00:29:26.220 --> 00:29:28.840
communicate COVID the way we communicated

00:29:28.840 --> 00:29:31.150
the swine flu pandemic in 2009.

00:29:31.150 --> 00:29:32.980
I mean, so if here was a pandemic

00:29:32.980 --> 00:29:35.280
that came into this country
and killed about 12,000 people.

00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:39.370
It was a worldwide
pandemic with this novel

00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:40.800
strain of influenza virus.

00:29:40.800 --> 00:29:44.710
About 2% of the worldwide
deaths occurred in this country.

00:29:44.710 --> 00:29:47.220
About a little more than 12,000
people died of that virus

00:29:47.220 --> 00:29:48.269
in this country.

00:29:48.269 --> 00:29:51.640
Every day, every other day,
there was Richard Besser,

00:29:51.640 --> 00:29:54.570
head of the CDC telling
you where things stood

00:29:54.570 --> 00:29:56.290
and why should it have been him

00:29:56.290 --> 00:29:58.470
because all the data you cared about,

00:29:58.470 --> 00:30:01.530
all the epidemiological
data came from the CDC

00:30:01.530 --> 00:30:04.150
didn't come from NIH, didn't
come from the administration,

00:30:04.150 --> 00:30:07.950
came from the CDC, also where
is the CDC, it's in Atlanta.

00:30:07.950 --> 00:30:10.690
So he was always giving his
conferences from Atlanta.

00:30:10.690 --> 00:30:13.710
Now, what you see is you see
these proclamations coming out

00:30:13.710 --> 00:30:16.830
of Washington and
therefore they are subject

00:30:16.830 --> 00:30:17.780
to political influence.

00:30:17.780 --> 00:30:20.210
I mean, if fantasies could
come true I would like to see

00:30:20.210 --> 00:30:22.530
Dr. Rochelle Walensky do all the talking

00:30:22.530 --> 00:30:24.550
out of her passion in Atlanta,

00:30:24.550 --> 00:30:26.340
because that's where we,
that's really all that

00:30:26.340 --> 00:30:29.670
the stuff's coming and
it's like radio silence.

00:30:29.670 --> 00:30:31.260
I mean, you don't hear anything.

00:30:31.260 --> 00:30:35.060
And what Besser understood
was that the media

00:30:35.060 --> 00:30:36.520
were the voices of the people.

00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:37.970
Those were the questions of the people

00:30:37.970 --> 00:30:38.803
that the people had to answer

00:30:38.803 --> 00:30:41.610
and he answered them
patiently every other day.

00:30:41.610 --> 00:30:44.080
It was great and we have
gotten away from that.

00:30:44.080 --> 00:30:46.840
And it's hard, I mean, I'm
only as a voting member

00:30:46.840 --> 00:30:48.170
of the FDA Vaccine Advisory Committee.

00:30:48.170 --> 00:30:49.630
It's hard to watch some of these things.

00:30:49.630 --> 00:30:51.139
I mean, it's not just
the Trump administration.

00:30:51.139 --> 00:30:54.210
When president Biden stood
up on August 18th and said,

00:30:54.210 --> 00:30:55.337
as of September 20th,

00:30:55.337 --> 00:30:59.030
we are going to have a
booster dose of COVID vaccine

00:30:59.030 --> 00:31:00.160
for everybody over 60.

00:31:00.160 --> 00:31:01.700
Where did that come from?

00:31:01.700 --> 00:31:04.580
I actually called a senior
official in the White House

00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:06.570
and said, where is this coming from?

00:31:06.570 --> 00:31:09.260
Where are the data that
drives that recommendation?

00:31:09.260 --> 00:31:10.093
And in fact,

00:31:10.093 --> 00:31:13.020
we kept pushing back on that
recommendation to Omicron hit,

00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:15.450
and then sort of the floodgate's
open for booster dosing.

00:31:15.450 --> 00:31:18.300
And I'm still a little lost
about for whom this is a two

00:31:18.300 --> 00:31:20.350
dose vaccine, for whom
it's a three dose vaccine,

00:31:20.350 --> 00:31:21.780
for whom it's a four dose vaccine

00:31:21.780 --> 00:31:23.890
and where boosters fit into any of this.

00:31:23.890 --> 00:31:25.880
Honestly, if you ask 10 Americans,

00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:27.460
what does it mean to be fully vaccinated?

00:31:27.460 --> 00:31:29.770
You'd probably get 10 different
answers because it's that

00:31:29.770 --> 00:31:31.970
confusing and I blame us
for that, I do, I think.

00:31:31.970 --> 00:31:34.360
- And that's not a general American issue,

00:31:34.360 --> 00:31:35.670
that's a doctor issue.

00:31:35.670 --> 00:31:37.040
Patients asking me the same.

00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:38.280
And depending on their age,

00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:40.780
I make like a clarification statement.

00:31:40.780 --> 00:31:42.810
But the reality is we
don't know, you know,

00:31:42.810 --> 00:31:45.740
nature had a good publication
showing a lot of efficacy

00:31:45.740 --> 00:31:48.380
for second booster for
those over the age of 60.

00:31:48.380 --> 00:31:51.750
But it matters that nuance matters.

00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:54.900
And I feel like nuance is lost,
especially on social media.

00:31:54.900 --> 00:31:57.760
I don't know how active you are
on Twitter and other sources

00:31:57.760 --> 00:31:59.710
in terms of reading
what others are saying.

00:31:59.710 --> 00:32:01.650
But the second you have disagreement,

00:32:01.650 --> 00:32:04.310
even amongst educational sources,

00:32:04.310 --> 00:32:06.410
whether it's someone from
Hopkins talking to someone from

00:32:06.410 --> 00:32:09.210
Stanford, if there is even a
small amount of disagreement,

00:32:09.210 --> 00:32:11.080
there's a lot of labeling that occurs

00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:13.700
where if you don't fully
stand with the FDA or CDC,

00:32:13.700 --> 00:32:15.410
you're critique for even one bit.

00:32:15.410 --> 00:32:18.070
It somehow means you're
taking an anti-vax stance

00:32:18.070 --> 00:32:20.830
or furthering the anti-vax agenda.

00:32:20.830 --> 00:32:23.390
Is that type of labeling necessary?

00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:27.510
Is it against what we're
trying to achieve in your eyes?

00:32:27.510 --> 00:32:28.644
- Well, of course, I mean,

00:32:28.644 --> 00:32:32.330
I think SNL, Saturday Night
Live had sort of a comedy skit

00:32:32.330 --> 00:32:34.070
on that, where you had
a group of sort of maybe

00:32:34.070 --> 00:32:36.180
three couples sitting
around a table in New York.

00:32:36.180 --> 00:32:38.550
And one of them started saying, you know,

00:32:38.550 --> 00:32:41.050
questioning whether or not
you really needed to mask

00:32:41.050 --> 00:32:43.030
in a particular situation.

00:32:43.030 --> 00:32:44.860
And then that person was vaporized.

00:32:44.860 --> 00:32:47.390
It was like, right you
can't question it all.

00:32:47.390 --> 00:32:48.750
Right now things are so confusing.

00:32:48.750 --> 00:32:51.380
I'm not sure well, what
exactly the story is.

00:32:51.380 --> 00:32:53.764
We, the committee, FDA Vaccine
Advisor Committee are gonna

00:32:53.764 --> 00:32:56.480
be meeting the end of
June to pick strengths

00:32:56.480 --> 00:32:58.563
for what I think they
want to have as a yearly,

00:32:58.563 --> 00:33:00.490
or at least every sort of late fall,

00:33:00.490 --> 00:33:01.560
early winter booster dose.

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:04.260
And I don't understand the
thinking there, I don't.

00:33:04.260 --> 00:33:06.690
I'm on the committee and
I'm supposed to be picking

00:33:06.690 --> 00:33:08.440
strengths and the way I see this,

00:33:08.440 --> 00:33:09.980
why do we get a yearly flu vaccine?

00:33:09.980 --> 00:33:11.990
We get a yearly flu vaccine
because even if you've been

00:33:11.990 --> 00:33:15.000
vaccinated or infected the year before,

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:16.490
you're still at risk for serious disease.

00:33:16.490 --> 00:33:19.261
For the most part protection
against serious disease holds

00:33:19.261 --> 00:33:21.020
up with this vaccine.

00:33:21.020 --> 00:33:25.200
I do think that for some this
is truly a three dose vaccine.

00:33:25.200 --> 00:33:27.610
I do, that third dose,

00:33:27.610 --> 00:33:30.490
when given four to six months
later increases your frequency

00:33:30.490 --> 00:33:31.550
of memory B and T socially,

00:33:31.550 --> 00:33:33.420
that you are better protected
against serious disease,

00:33:33.420 --> 00:33:35.840
and that's the immune component
associated with protection

00:33:35.840 --> 00:33:36.730
against serious disease,

00:33:36.730 --> 00:33:38.850
people over 65, people
who have comorbidities.

00:33:38.850 --> 00:33:43.260
I still can't quite fathom the
clear evidence that a healthy

00:33:43.260 --> 00:33:46.320
less than 50 year old really
benefits from a third dose

00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:48.140
in terms of protection
against serious illness,

00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:50.300
which is the goal, unless
that's not the goal,

00:33:50.300 --> 00:33:52.280
unless the goal is
preventing mild illness.

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:54.100
In which case we're gonna
have to keep boosting

00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:57.390
because neutralized, again,
buys, always fade at some level

00:33:57.390 --> 00:33:59.160
three or six months after a vaccination.

00:33:59.160 --> 00:34:01.390
So is that the goal in which
case we're always gonna be

00:34:01.390 --> 00:34:05.060
boosting, which is great
news for pharma companies.

00:34:05.060 --> 00:34:07.612
I'm just not sure it's
necessarily good news for us.

00:34:07.612 --> 00:34:12.612
- Is there any truth to the
fact that if we decrease

00:34:12.900 --> 00:34:15.360
the likelihood of
developing mild infections,

00:34:15.360 --> 00:34:19.000
that we decrease new
strains from coming about?

00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:20.970
- Well, first of all, good luck with that.

00:34:20.970 --> 00:34:23.530
I mean, this is a short
incubation period disease.

00:34:23.530 --> 00:34:26.300
The viremia virus spread in
the bloodstream is not an

00:34:26.300 --> 00:34:28.300
important part of the disease process

00:34:28.300 --> 00:34:31.200
for these kinds of short
incubation period diseases.

00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:33.210
The goal is to, the only reasonable goal,

00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:35.740
the only achievable goal is
to prevent really moderate

00:34:35.740 --> 00:34:38.120
to severe. So I was fortunate
enough to be part of a team

00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:39.540
at Children's Hospital in Philadelphia.

00:34:39.540 --> 00:34:41.860
They created the strains that
became the rotavirus vaccine

00:34:41.860 --> 00:34:43.770
rota attack, that was a 26 year effort.

00:34:43.770 --> 00:34:45.840
I am the co inventor of
the rotavirus vaccine.

00:34:45.840 --> 00:34:48.250
That is a mucosal
infection like SARS-CoV-2,

00:34:48.250 --> 00:34:52.180
meaning short incubation period
infects of mucosal surface.

00:34:52.180 --> 00:34:53.670
When you have short incubation periods,

00:34:53.670 --> 00:34:56.410
you are not going to be able
to protect for any length

00:34:56.410 --> 00:34:58.540
of time against mild
asymptomatic infection.

00:34:58.540 --> 00:35:01.310
I mean, we have eliminated
essentially with our vaccine

00:35:01.310 --> 00:35:04.630
hospitalizations in babies from
rotavirus, we've done that,

00:35:04.630 --> 00:35:06.410
but the virus still
circulates in the community.

00:35:06.410 --> 00:35:08.330
That's gonna be true here too.

00:35:08.330 --> 00:35:09.860
We're not gonna prevent mild disease.

00:35:09.860 --> 00:35:11.450
And so I think what
people worry about now,

00:35:11.450 --> 00:35:13.130
well was if it's true,
if I get mild disease,

00:35:13.130 --> 00:35:14.410
can I still get long COVID?

00:35:14.410 --> 00:35:16.700
And I don't wanna get a mild disease

00:35:16.700 --> 00:35:20.210
and even people on the CDC
Advisory Committee just last week

00:35:20.210 --> 00:35:23.090
said, we have to have a better
vaccine against mild disease.

00:35:23.090 --> 00:35:24.770
Well, if you want a better
vaccine against mild disease,

00:35:24.770 --> 00:35:26.530
figure out a way to lengthen
the incubation period,

00:35:26.530 --> 00:35:28.860
because otherwise you're
gonna have trouble doing that.

00:35:28.860 --> 00:35:30.230
It's just, it's hard to watch.

00:35:30.230 --> 00:35:33.400
I think coming off this zero
tolerance strategy for COVID,

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:35.320
we're gonna have to realize
mild disease is gonna be part

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:37.400
of this for the rest of our lives.

00:35:37.400 --> 00:35:39.940
I mean, this virus is
gonna circulate for decades

00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:42.210
and it's gonna continue
to cause mild illness.

00:35:42.210 --> 00:35:44.890
And even if the entire
world were vaccinated,

00:35:44.890 --> 00:35:46.020
that would still be true.

00:35:46.020 --> 00:35:48.090
And I don't think people
quite understand that.

00:35:48.090 --> 00:35:51.480
- State medical boards exist
to keep doctors ethically

00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:52.980
and legally in check.

00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:56.130
Yet too often, doctors get
away with placing profits

00:35:56.130 --> 00:35:57.240
over patients.

00:35:57.240 --> 00:35:59.680
Considering Dr. Offit,
is well versed in the art

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:02.030
of the snake oil salesman I asked him,

00:36:02.030 --> 00:36:04.670
do you think medical boards
should be taking a more

00:36:04.670 --> 00:36:08.500
proactive stance here in sort
of disciplinary action wise?

00:36:08.500 --> 00:36:10.300
- Yes, I do.

00:36:10.300 --> 00:36:11.219
And they don't.

00:36:11.219 --> 00:36:12.052
I mean, I'm right now,

00:36:12.052 --> 00:36:14.990
I'm an Avalon New Jersey three
blocks from now, from here,

00:36:14.990 --> 00:36:18.350
there is an IV vitamin treatment center.

00:36:18.350 --> 00:36:19.860
It's actually right next to a bar.

00:36:19.860 --> 00:36:22.610
And one of the ways that they
promote themselves is to say

00:36:22.610 --> 00:36:26.310
kind of detox yourself
after drinking too much.

00:36:26.310 --> 00:36:28.530
Yeah, I mean, I think the,

00:36:28.530 --> 00:36:31.390
I think as generally licensing agencies,

00:36:31.390 --> 00:36:33.360
ethics boards are terrible.

00:36:33.360 --> 00:36:36.190
We are terrible as physicians
about pleasing ourselves,

00:36:36.190 --> 00:36:38.490
terrible and so who pleases us.

00:36:38.490 --> 00:36:41.160
In theory, lawyers please us, but there,

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:43.680
they don't really sue
so much for bad care,

00:36:43.680 --> 00:36:45.450
as much as they sue for bad outcomes,

00:36:45.450 --> 00:36:46.500
which are always gonna be true.

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:48.840
So that's not an effective
way to please us.

00:36:48.840 --> 00:36:50.800
No, I think you're exactly right or people

00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:54.571
who recommend against
vaccines or, you know, but it,

00:36:54.571 --> 00:36:57.040
and it's all marketing, right?

00:36:57.040 --> 00:36:58.930
I mean, I think that some
physicians realize there is,

00:36:58.930 --> 00:37:01.500
this is, they can with
a boutique practice,

00:37:01.500 --> 00:37:03.050
you can look like you care.

00:37:03.050 --> 00:37:04.630
You're buying into the zeitgeist here

00:37:04.630 --> 00:37:07.250
these magic pills that will
make you healthier and better

00:37:07.250 --> 00:37:09.120
and have better sex and thicker hair,

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:10.520
whatever it is that they're promoting.

00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:12.780
And it's hard to watch and we are terrible

00:37:14.197 --> 00:37:16.193
at really regulating ourselves here.

00:37:16.193 --> 00:37:18.480
And that's why everybody
gets away with it.

00:37:18.480 --> 00:37:21.100
- Yeah, like I thought that by
starting my YouTube channel,

00:37:21.100 --> 00:37:23.550
reaching millions of people,
I mean, monthly, we get 70,

00:37:23.550 --> 00:37:26.440
80 million viewers on our YouTube channel.

00:37:26.440 --> 00:37:30.110
And I thought if I could talk
about why there's no evidence

00:37:30.110 --> 00:37:33.390
for some of these things or
why I don't believe they work

00:37:33.390 --> 00:37:35.830
and explain the science behind
it, people would listen.

00:37:35.830 --> 00:37:38.545
And while some people do the
frequent pushback I get is

00:37:38.545 --> 00:37:40.270
you're a young doctor.

00:37:40.270 --> 00:37:41.760
You didn't go to an Ivy League School.

00:37:41.760 --> 00:37:44.456
You don't understand the
science that this person

00:37:44.456 --> 00:37:46.290
is talking about.

00:37:46.290 --> 00:37:48.550
But when I've even been
approached by these companies

00:37:48.550 --> 00:37:49.720
to promote their product,

00:37:49.720 --> 00:37:52.440
I would love to promote
a product that cures,

00:37:52.440 --> 00:37:54.400
like some of the illnesses
that they talk about,

00:37:54.400 --> 00:37:57.180
because I deal with them in
my practice and I see how much

00:37:57.180 --> 00:37:58.550
they hurt my patients.

00:37:58.550 --> 00:38:00.640
I would love to have a pill to say,

00:38:00.640 --> 00:38:03.420
oh, you have irritable
bowel syndrome that destroys

00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:05.750
your life, here is a
probiotic to solve it.

00:38:05.750 --> 00:38:07.070
It just doesn't exist.

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:08.680
And when the companies come to me,

00:38:08.680 --> 00:38:11.170
they flood me with
10,000 pages of research.

00:38:11.170 --> 00:38:14.660
And when I really spend the
hours looking at the research,

00:38:14.660 --> 00:38:17.570
they don't even prove that
their probiotic pill works.

00:38:17.570 --> 00:38:20.380
They prove that their
probiotic pill survives

00:38:20.380 --> 00:38:22.580
in the acidic environment in the stomach.

00:38:22.580 --> 00:38:25.090
And somehow that means it works.

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:28.830
But the reality is they make
you look at the cool stuff

00:38:28.830 --> 00:38:30.920
on one hand, but don't
really substantiate it

00:38:30.920 --> 00:38:32.280
with anything else.

00:38:32.280 --> 00:38:36.420
And I feel almost powerless
to attack it because you can't

00:38:36.420 --> 00:38:37.810
attack something like you said,

00:38:37.810 --> 00:38:38.750
in the beginning of this interview

00:38:38.750 --> 00:38:42.000
that you can't say with
definite proof does not work.

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:43.570
I can't say with a hundred percent proof,

00:38:43.570 --> 00:38:44.930
those probiotics don't work.

00:38:44.930 --> 00:38:47.110
I could say, there's no
evidence that they work.

00:38:47.110 --> 00:38:50.630
How do we attack this
industry more effectively?

00:38:50.630 --> 00:38:52.570
- I think we at the very
least, we have to show that

00:38:52.570 --> 00:38:53.840
there are downsides.

00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:55.610
That anything that has a positive effect

00:38:55.610 --> 00:38:57.970
can have a negative effect
and that you can see now

00:38:57.970 --> 00:38:59.480
with the, cause I think
people don't know that.

00:38:59.480 --> 00:39:00.580
People don't know that for example,

00:39:00.580 --> 00:39:02.950
if you take these high
quantities of vitamin C that you

00:39:02.950 --> 00:39:05.260
increase your risk of hit
kidney stones, for example.

00:39:05.260 --> 00:39:08.710
And that can be serious as
just one of many examples.

00:39:08.710 --> 00:39:11.460
And I think people don't, this con,

00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:13.950
this industry has gotten
away with this notion,

00:39:13.950 --> 00:39:16.050
this false notion that it's all positive

00:39:16.050 --> 00:39:17.140
and nothing bad can happen.

00:39:17.140 --> 00:39:18.610
That's never true in medicine.

00:39:18.610 --> 00:39:20.880
If there's, if something
doesn't have a negative effect,

00:39:20.880 --> 00:39:22.490
it probably never had a positive effect.

00:39:22.490 --> 00:39:24.202
And I just think we need
to pull the curtain back

00:39:24.202 --> 00:39:27.380
because I do think that works
at some level when people see

00:39:27.380 --> 00:39:30.610
some of the fairies nature of
the way that this all works.

00:39:30.610 --> 00:39:33.110
But I would like to say one
thing in case we're gonna end

00:39:33.110 --> 00:39:36.120
soon, is I am really happy
there are people like you

00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:36.953
out there.

00:39:36.953 --> 00:39:40.040
I mean, young people who
are skeptical as physicians

00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:42.100
that really are looking
behind the curtain here.

00:39:42.100 --> 00:39:44.820
It is heartening to me to
know that you're out there.

00:39:44.820 --> 00:39:47.550
Thank you for being out there.

00:39:47.550 --> 00:39:50.920
- Well, honestly, inspired
by you and your skepticism,

00:39:50.920 --> 00:39:52.540
because I always feel in medicine,

00:39:52.540 --> 00:39:55.010
you need to have a very
strong balance between being

00:39:55.010 --> 00:39:58.330
a healthy skeptic and not
disbelieving any new innovation

00:39:58.330 --> 00:39:59.520
in technology,

00:39:59.520 --> 00:40:01.810
because it's very easy to fall
into that trap where anything

00:40:01.810 --> 00:40:03.950
new is bad and we don't
want to go that route.

00:40:03.950 --> 00:40:07.370
And at the same time to say
anything revolutionary must

00:40:07.370 --> 00:40:08.690
remove everything that we've done.

00:40:08.690 --> 00:40:11.580
That's time tested and proved and proven.

00:40:11.580 --> 00:40:12.450
So to me,

00:40:12.450 --> 00:40:14.670
I actually just did an interview
for Medscape the other day

00:40:14.670 --> 00:40:16.790
about the differences
between older physicians

00:40:16.790 --> 00:40:17.910
and younger physicians.

00:40:17.910 --> 00:40:19.970
And the answer wasn't one or the other.

00:40:19.970 --> 00:40:21.470
I don't prefer one or the other.

00:40:21.470 --> 00:40:24.050
In fact, it's the collaborative
approach of the two

00:40:24.050 --> 00:40:26.260
let's learn what worked over the years.

00:40:26.260 --> 00:40:27.640
Let's take the younger approach,

00:40:27.640 --> 00:40:29.570
how we can make technology work with us

00:40:29.570 --> 00:40:30.830
instead of against us,

00:40:30.830 --> 00:40:33.970
but not sell out to these
hedge fund companies

00:40:33.970 --> 00:40:38.790
that wanna run medicine in a
way that makes the checkbook

00:40:38.790 --> 00:40:40.510
get a little thinner,
get the wallet thinner,

00:40:40.510 --> 00:40:42.110
as opposed to our waste thinner.

00:40:43.610 --> 00:40:46.490
To me, that's the most
disheartening thing.

00:40:46.490 --> 00:40:50.520
I think that medicine is
becoming to be a hedge fund

00:40:50.520 --> 00:40:51.710
in the business world.

00:40:51.710 --> 00:40:55.700
And that happens even in the
telemedicine front, you'll see,

00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:59.190
like we had to go virtual for
the first few months of COVID

00:40:59.190 --> 00:41:00.550
because our office shut down.

00:41:00.550 --> 00:41:03.360
And I saw how ineffective
this was in so many

00:41:03.360 --> 00:41:04.751
of my patient's cases.

00:41:04.751 --> 00:41:07.560
Good luck treating or figuring
out abdominal pain through

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:11.239
a virtual exam, virtually
worthless, I would say.

00:41:11.239 --> 00:41:13.410
But there were some utility to it.

00:41:13.410 --> 00:41:16.250
And now what I see online is
all these companies popping up,

00:41:16.250 --> 00:41:17.270
do a virtual visit,

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:19.460
five minutes with our
doctor will give you Viagra,

00:41:19.460 --> 00:41:22.230
will give you antibiotics,
will give you Propecia.

00:41:22.230 --> 00:41:25.710
Will make your hair grow thicker
with no checking to see is

00:41:25.710 --> 00:41:27.570
this patient having erectile dysfunction

00:41:27.570 --> 00:41:29.460
because of severe diabetes.

00:41:29.460 --> 00:41:33.430
Is this patient having a
fungal infection under scalp

00:41:33.430 --> 00:41:34.910
and that's why they're losing hair.

00:41:34.910 --> 00:41:37.820
And all of these things are
sort of corrupting medicine.

00:41:37.820 --> 00:41:40.970
And I wanna be the one
pressing the brakes and saying,

00:41:40.970 --> 00:41:45.240
let's be good marketers and
see what marketers do well,

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:47.650
but push the evidence based approach

00:41:47.650 --> 00:41:49.560
with the marketing, spin on it.

00:41:49.560 --> 00:41:52.910
And that's sort of an optimistic,
maybe unrealistic goal

00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.860
that I've had with my YouTube channel.

00:41:54.860 --> 00:41:56.290
I don't know what your
take on that would be.

00:41:56.290 --> 00:41:58.856
- Now, I think that's absolutely
great, I congratulate.

00:41:58.856 --> 00:42:03.470
I think it's a, skepticism
is healthy, a cynicism isn't

00:42:03.470 --> 00:42:06.570
and so be open-minded to
the day to the fact that

00:42:06.570 --> 00:42:08.960
there may be data that
contradicts something you believe

00:42:08.960 --> 00:42:11.150
is true, have believed it was true.

00:42:11.150 --> 00:42:13.790
But don't be so cynical that
you don't believe clear,

00:42:13.790 --> 00:42:15.660
compelling, reproducible data.

00:42:15.660 --> 00:42:17.900
- Frequently patients
and friends will claim

00:42:17.900 --> 00:42:19.760
that they've done their research,

00:42:19.760 --> 00:42:21.820
which usually means they
did a quick Google search

00:42:21.820 --> 00:42:23.000
or read a Facebook thread.

00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:25.070
With everyone these days,
considering themselves,

00:42:25.070 --> 00:42:26.570
some sort of expert.

00:42:26.570 --> 00:42:28.990
I had to ask him in
your book, "Bad Advice"

00:42:28.990 --> 00:42:31.480
you talked about how you
shouldn't take for the average

00:42:31.480 --> 00:42:34.850
person, shouldn't take advice
from politicians, celebrities,

00:42:34.850 --> 00:42:37.260
activists, who should
they take advice from?

00:42:37.260 --> 00:42:40.410
- Well, you know it's the experts.

00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:42.880
I mean, it's, we don't like that term,

00:42:42.880 --> 00:42:44.620
this now in the 21st century, you know,

00:42:44.620 --> 00:42:45.730
trust me I'm an expert,

00:42:45.730 --> 00:42:48.130
that's not exactly something it sells.

00:42:48.130 --> 00:42:50.300
But that is true when people say to me

00:42:50.300 --> 00:42:53.450
I've done my research on
the chickenpox vaccine

00:42:53.450 --> 00:42:54.560
and I've decided not to get it.

00:42:54.560 --> 00:42:56.570
Well, what do they really
mean by do their research?

00:42:56.570 --> 00:42:58.530
What they really mean is
they've read people's opinions

00:42:58.530 --> 00:43:00.170
about the vaccine on the internet.

00:43:00.170 --> 00:43:01.780
I mean, if they really
wanna do their research

00:43:01.780 --> 00:43:03.870
on the chickenpox vaccine,
well, they should do,

00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:06.320
they should read the roughly
300 papers that have been

00:43:06.320 --> 00:43:08.120
published on the vaccine,

00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:11.260
which would require some
expertise in virology, immunology,

00:43:11.260 --> 00:43:13.450
epidemiology, et cetera.

00:43:13.450 --> 00:43:14.820
Most people don't have that expertise.

00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:16.560
Frankly, most doctors
don't have that expertise.

00:43:16.560 --> 00:43:17.400
So what do they do?

00:43:17.400 --> 00:43:22.030
They rely on expert advisory bodies, like,

00:43:22.030 --> 00:43:25.070
FDA Advisory Committees
and CDC Advisory Committees

00:43:25.070 --> 00:43:27.040
that at least collectively
have read those papers,

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:30.270
collectively have an expertise
to evaluate those papers.

00:43:30.270 --> 00:43:32.520
And then collectively make
a decision about whether

00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:34.100
the vaccine is of value.

00:43:34.100 --> 00:43:36.140
But you know that people
just don't do that.

00:43:36.140 --> 00:43:36.973
And you can't,

00:43:36.973 --> 00:43:40.370
it's dismissive these days to
say anything like, you know,

00:43:40.370 --> 00:43:45.370
you really should rely on
informed opinions based on data

00:43:45.450 --> 00:43:47.380
doesn't work because
people believe they can be

00:43:47.380 --> 00:43:50.670
just informed by Googling the
word VA, chickenpox vaccine

00:43:50.670 --> 00:43:52.800
as anybody else which isn't true.

00:43:52.800 --> 00:43:56.610
And I just, you know, so try
and explain that to people.

00:43:56.610 --> 00:43:57.443
It's hard.

00:43:57.443 --> 00:43:58.734
I mean, it is hard.

00:43:58.734 --> 00:44:01.220
- I think I share some
empathy for the average member

00:44:01.220 --> 00:44:03.520
of the public, because we
say to look to the CDC,

00:44:03.520 --> 00:44:08.120
the FDA for guidance, and you
sit on the ACIP committee.

00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:11.190
And yet you're saying that
the FDA's pushing some things

00:44:11.190 --> 00:44:13.150
along that you just
frankly don't agree with

00:44:13.150 --> 00:44:15.330
and it's confusing to
how it's gotten there.

00:44:15.330 --> 00:44:16.870
- Well, I sit on the
FDA committee actually.

00:44:16.870 --> 00:44:18.590
I used to be on the CDC.

00:44:18.590 --> 00:44:20.090
So I've been on both
committees, you're right.

00:44:20.090 --> 00:44:22.100
And I think what happens
is it's not the committees

00:44:22.100 --> 00:44:22.933
that are the problem.

00:44:22.933 --> 00:44:25.630
It's when the administration
bypasses the committee.

00:44:25.630 --> 00:44:28.690
When president Biden stood
up in August of last year

00:44:28.690 --> 00:44:31.090
and said, we're gonna offer
booster doses for everybody.

00:44:31.090 --> 00:44:35.330
He bypassed the FDA and
bypassed the CDC, that's bad.

00:44:35.330 --> 00:44:36.740
That's a bad thing to do.

00:44:36.740 --> 00:44:41.400
- So we as medical
experts should keep church

00:44:41.400 --> 00:44:45.030
and state separate in the
sense of church being science

00:44:45.030 --> 00:44:46.850
and state being government,

00:44:46.850 --> 00:44:49.870
because it's very clear
how that undo influence

00:44:49.870 --> 00:44:52.890
cannot only directly
harm those institutions,

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:54.330
but also hurt the public trust.

00:44:54.330 --> 00:44:55.880
- Yes, I agree.

00:44:55.880 --> 00:44:57.440
- Natural remedies aren't all bad.

00:44:57.440 --> 00:45:00.390
In fact, here, I've compiled
a list of 10 natural remedies

00:45:00.390 --> 00:45:01.410
that actually work.

